- **Command line (`escher-session`, unix only; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli):** each driver command is run as a process of the package's own binary against a host its `start` command spawned — `cli_commands` (14): each of the four tasks starts, answers and stops; `snapshot --part` read by number answers one uncoloured JSON line, status 0, and `--part` 0, 1001 and `x` exit 1 with a line equal to `Refusal::malformed(fault).to_json()`, nothing typed written back (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:294-339); since 2026-10-14-quality-gates a run with its stdout closed before it starts keeps its ending's status — `help` 0, `snapshot` with no session 3 with exactly `NoSession`'s message — printing no panic and writing nothing typed back (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:675-700); each of the eight instance-level verbs is accepted and answers exactly its fields — since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a `screenshot` answering status `0` and one line whose `png`, decoded by a hand base64 reader and checked by its PNG header, equals the PNG `Session::run` returns in process (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:341-413); a hosted `lint` answers status `0` and one line `{"findings":[]}` (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:414-435); a snapshot is the in-process text as one line inside its 10,000-byte budget (832 · 1,393 · 1,368 · 2,202 bytes on the four tasks, line break included, by hand smoke at 2026-10-10-snapshot-states; 832 · 1,375 · 1,368 · 2,187 before it); a call a target cannot take is refused with its cause, status `1`; a call the schema refuses reaches no session; a command with no session is a session error, status `3`; a line that is no command is a usage error, status `2`; Tab on a fresh boot moves focus to `back-btn` alone;
 since 2026-10-12-self-description `help` answers status `0` and one line equal to `describe()`, reaching no session, every cause the binary provokes (`unknown-verb`, `malformed`, `disabled`, `not-found`, `off-screen`, `stale`) reads `remedy` equal to its cause's, and a state directory of 94 bytes as given starts and stops while one of 95 ends `state-dir-too-long`, status `3`, its message naming 94 and its remedy the table's, and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, off Linux one of 90 bytes starts and stops while one of 91 ends `state-dir-too-long`, status `3`, with no path in the message — its one witness the fork's CI run on the macOS leg, CI#38642493451, job 116123587286, `cli_commands` 11 passed on `aarch64-apple-darwin` (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:708-712) — `cli_flow` (2): the two shell flows `counter.sh` (8 steps) and `flight.sh` (7) complete under plain `sh` and leave nothing, and a flow handed a binary that answers nothing says which step failed and stops its session — and `host_timer` (1): the timer host moved by a hosted `advance` with no sleep, reporting exactly the `ms` asked; the fork's CI run on the macOS leg is the one witness of the select-all modifier and of the two flows there (examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:129-606; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:607-781; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_flow.rs:31-88; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_timer.rs:22-126; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/report.md, the two new tests at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-self-description/report.md);
 since 2026-10-19-session-recording `start <task> --record <dir>` run as a process keeps one `0600` check in a `0700` directory, the state directory gone after `stop`, a group-open recording directory refused status `3` with nothing spawned (seven_guis `recording`), and `cli_commands` reads the usage line naming `--record` on `start`, the host role and the `mcp` role, a misplaced `--record` a usage error, status `2`, and since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay `recording`'s `the_committed_checks_are_what_the_binary_records` runs `record_checks.sh` — a command-line session (`start counter --record` · `snapshot` · `click counter-increment` · `advance 600` · `click counter-increment` · `snapshot` · `stop`) and an MCP one (`initialize` … `scroll counter-increment` · `snapshot` · `stop`) — through the binary and reads both kept checks byte-equal to `tests/blitz-tests/checks/counter-{cli,mcp}.json`, the scripts holding no `screenshot` step since a shot's PNG bytes differ by OS (CI#39225375577) (examples/seven_guis/tests/recording.rs:205-262; examples/seven_guis/tests/recording.rs:264-304; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:576-586)
